   "ResearcherNotesUnit": "GC, Aug 2026: Moving from proposed to shelved-inferred. There's been no news about this project since Dec 2024, other than a passing mention in an Apr 2026 article from BNAmericas: \"Otros proyectos de importación incluyen... la instalación de US$542 millones de Nevo FSRU Jambelí en Ecuador...\". \nMeanwhile, owner Sycar's website has not been updated since June 2022, and still shows a 2025 start date, which is obviously incorrect. My sense is that the project has been abandoned, but it seems prudent to keep it as shelved-inferred for another couple of cycles, then move to cancelled-inferred if no news during that period.\n\nBL, June 2025: looks like it was last mentioned in Nov/Dec of 2024, so it's still technically under the 2y shelved-inferred threshold for us. Keep it as proposed. I added 2 more refs to proposed.\nAL, Jul 2025: I also think this project is most likely shelved, although I found one mention of it from Dec 2024, so I'm leaving it as proposed. However, it seems SYCAR is mostly focusing on land-based LNG imports for now, and I see no indications of construction or any other activities related to the FSRU commissioning. https://informationstreamer.com/2024/12/02/sycars-historic-lng-import-from-peru-marks-major-energy-milestone-for-ecuador/ \nGC, Aug 2024: No signs of project moving forward during the past 13 months -- move to Shelved in 2025 if no further progress?; Gregor, July 2023: FSRU not due to operate until 2025, but an FSU (without regasification capability) may start up as early as 2023.",
